  <static seed="250" source="Library/Michigan/Chap3Sec6/Q25.pg">
    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function <m>f(x)</m>, below.  It may be to
your advantage to simplify before differentiating.</p>
<p><m>f(x) = \cos(\arctan(3 x))</m></p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="65" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1\cdot 3\sin\mathopen{}\left(\tan^{-1}\mathopen{}\left(3x\right)\right)}{1+\left(3x\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f'(x) = \frac{-3 \sin(\arctan(3 x))}{1 + (3 x)^2} = \frac{-3 \sin(\arctan(3 x))}{1 + 9 x^2}</m>



</solution>
